{"step_index":106,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-07T20:25:26Z","thinking":"**Defining API Routers Structure**\n\nThe API routers need defining to establish endpoints. Health check will require a simple GET endpoint. Cases will need GET, GET with an ID, and POST endpoints.\n\nNetwork data will use case IDs, similar to entities and insights. Finally, an aggregating router will combine the sub-routers.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"\"\"\"Health check router.\"\"\"\nfrom fastapi import APIRouter\nfrom app.schemas.common import HealthResponse\nfrom app.utils.config import settings\nfrom app.services.mock_data import SYNTHETIC_DATASET_LABEL\n\nrouter = APIRouter(tags=[\"Health\"])\n\n\n@router.get(\n    \"/health\",\n    response_model=HealthResponse,\n    summary=\"Service Health Check\",\n    description=\"Returns the operational status of the NEXUS Intelligence API and dataset compliance metadata.\"\n)\nasync def health_check():\n    return HealthResponse(\n        status=\"healthy\",\n        service=settings.PROJECT_NAME,\n        version=settings.VERSION,\n        dataset=SYNTHETIC_DATASET_LABEL,\n        active_cases=1\n    )\n","Description":"Create api/health.py","Overwrite":true,"TargetFile":"C:\\Users\\Nityam Jaiswal\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\backend\\app\\api\\health.py","toolAction":"Writing health.py router","toolSummary":"Create app/api/health.py"}}]}
